{
  "schema": "rh-independent-mathematical-review/1",
  "artifact_version": "0.55",
  "component": "stabilizer_volume_v55",
  "reviewer": "root",
  "author": "bessel_nonvanishing",
  "source_commit": "7cbf7a0c32fca1badf05931879a37c3f8a2b03b4",
  "status": "PASS",
  "proof_file_sha256": "358b9ff25062d7b74218b154105b17dfbcd219ad930a6715318cb6bdb42dfebd",
  "claims_reviewed": [
    {
      "id": "SVW1",
      "block_sha256": "05582ee1812315011b638dfbdf02d926d45bafa5ee53b22461c197d92a3a6b57",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The finite-coordinate restricted-product topology is locally compact and second countable. The rational diagonal is closed discrete by its integral lattice at infinity. The unitary equations define a closed subset with continuous inverse, and the stabilizer is closed; rational matrix subgroups are countable and discrete. Thus the actual Haar measures are Radon and sigma-finite."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW2",
      "block_sha256": "4b2ceff0c6cd33df5b8748295170c9990dc5542b3e80d90adf50ad000bc08d2c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "An admissible pure test is supported in a product with only finitely many exceptional finite factors. That product lies in a clopen restricted-product chart, so extension by zero is continuous and support is compact. Arbitrary compact sets admit larger finite boxes and a smooth infinite cutoff. Compactness plus the rational closed-discrete set gives the full FinTheta scope, and a countable sum gives measurability."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW3",
      "block_sha256": "5aa0c554f8ae150e3c13e221b29e0dd0380506b0229581290e0a19cefdfd69f3",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Every supplied IsOmT includes actual integrability for every admissible test. Admissible cutoffs therefore prove local finiteness of that supplied measure before Radon uniqueness is used. Compact-open finite boxes times compact infinite tests determine the Borel measure. This proves uniqueness for every IsOmT and closes the universal supplied-measure requirement in ExStab; an existential compatible pair alone would not suffice."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW4",
      "block_sha256": "6d9c397b51a674f5be985658225657ae035b739fda8b713bd0989400283f98fd",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "A compact Hermitian cutoff supported in the invertible locus puts the tuple test inside the independent locus. The full fiber-family continuity then gives a continuous density near the specified T. Equality of compact-set integrals and positive Haar mass force pointwise equality of continuous complex densities. This preserves every supplied local witness and proves fixed-T equality rather than only an almost-everywhere statement."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW5",
      "block_sha256": "b515f86dd0627db8bdee8b5d0f9654a29f8da2bd257514148d225417e9e03c2d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Compact support implies the literal rapid-decay inequality for every exponent. The smooth compatibility premise is specialized using the same IsOmT self-dual witnesses, character, ambient Haar and domain. Pointwise local density identification and the stated convergent products give SWeqOm without rearranging a product or changing normalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW6",
      "block_sha256": "2096fcac405da528150190514ef6905cb7f974e4b12f5c4ae26d7c82095cc7ea",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The nondegenerate rational Gram spans are isometric. The displayed Hermitian rank-one map has denominator d=h(u-v,u), sends u to v and preserves the form because h(u-v,u-v)=d+conjugate(d). If d=0 the u,-v construction has denominator 2t, followed by negation on the current orthogonal complement. The construction fixes earlier lines and remains rational. Right cosets Gamma/Delta count each rational tuple exactly once."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW7",
      "block_sha256": "ca4a9b5914d600aefb4b7a9755d9244b882ff7168fc599c0f9ba5b99554ff161",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The translates U x_j each intersect a left discrete-subgroup orbit at most once because UU^{-1} meets the subgroup only at identity. Selecting the first chart gives a Borel strict domain. No quotient mass assumption enters, so ExFDStab is proved before finite stabilizer mass."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW8",
      "block_sha256": "492953b316ab88c7b78969581319ef89da69d155d0c950715f2f94761c8abeb3",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Null-measurable source domains have measurable representatives; countability and invariant measure preserve all translated almost-everywhere identities. Inserting the translated indicator sum and using nonnegative Tonelli proves domain independence even at infinite mass. The analogous right-domain statement is legitimate once the measure is right invariant."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW9",
      "block_sha256": "ee8825d4ed17f124d678cffdb00ec595781b3bef24717ae48d90fb4c78b4b471",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Local unitary unimodularity follows from the nondegenerate invariant trace pairing; at infinity its real form has determinant of absolute value one. Restricted-product cylinder checks then give a bi-invariant adelic Haar measure, and uniqueness transports to every supplied normalization. The nondegenerate pointwise stabilizer is the rational orthogonal-complement unitary group. Inversion invariance is fixed by a symmetric positive finite compact neighborhood."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW10",
      "block_sha256": "1263acf2220e8ddcd8d389bb3409da805019aaeae7aba26c1566d3c489e409bd",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The right-coset convention is correct: Gamma is the disjoint union of Delta gamma^{-1}, so the union of gamma^{-1}D is a left Delta domain and its inverse a right Delta domain. In each fiber s(y)H the set of h landing in that inverse domain is a right Delta domain. Its mass is the same stabilizer covolume, possibly infinite. Compatibility and nonnegative integrals prove unfolding before any finite-mass conversion."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW11",
      "block_sha256": "ea9abfad2c0a783fabc18c1bcfd838aec7691c22ed92e15acd4b7f93f999bdb8",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The nonzero complex Bochner theta integral rules out its nonintegrable zero fallback. The nonnegative integral is therefore finite and strictly positive. IsOmT supplies finite integral I of the test; extended unfolding gives 0<L=mass(F_H)*I<infinity. Only then are I>0 and finite stabilizer mass deduced and real values taken. Thus no cancellation of the real value of an infinite measure occurs."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW12",
      "block_sha256": "cff7a0a55685a36a8bfea3970fe39f7e74b5c26b2f26e63bcebb369307789e3c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "One rational scalar clears the finitely many denominators of X0 in a fixed E/F basis. The corresponding tuple lattice is open compact in the finite restricted product and contains X0 at all finite places. A smooth positive compact bump at infinity gives one admissible all-chart-smooth product. Its positivity pulls back to a genuine open identity neighborhood in G."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW13",
      "block_sha256": "e9711cf286ea65f1215bc50384f141dc23d9ba8649ba1efacc0f5315b115965b",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "IsOmT gives finite integral. If its nonnegative integral vanished, compatibility applied to the identity-neighborhood indicator would force positive Haar mass of that neighborhood to vanish: every fiber with zero test value contributes zero. This proves positivity for every supplied compatible measure, with the same test used in the density and unfolding equations."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW14",
      "block_sha256": "1b33e6d355e4d8f9af17a8082bf78f2dd08d5143cdb41089bf5b0f4e7baac9c2",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Character and IsOmT existence reuse the already proved GMR records. SVW3 identifies an arbitrary supplied IsOmT with the constructed positive Radon orbit measure, so GMR11 supplies a compatible Haar measure for that arbitrary witness. SVW7 gives every stabilizer domain stage. Ambient domains and finite mass use exactly SWa1. The six nested existence/universality stages are preserved."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW15",
      "block_sha256": "58274ce9b4d85c50e7743755b30aece9fbb7fe6f7c7d5d8ec5c57ac5c86df428",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The ambient domain has positive finite mass by SWa1 and countable translates. SWeqOm with the same positive test gives a nonzero theta integral; Unfold then gives finite stabilizer mass. Cancellation is now between positive finite real scalars, and the finite extended masses are equal. Original SWa1 and StabilizerFirstChernCompatibility remain premises, not renamed conclusions."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW16",
      "block_sha256": "458efcb9be3c8532837ae305135cf48f89963b82f1d231373b342b6bc1d6d77a",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The rational stabilizer subgroups ratOf and ratIn agree by literal inverse-image membership. The chosen covolume domains exist, and the universal VolStabW equality applies to those precise choices. Equality of real values holds even for an arbitrary supplied VolStabW without finite-mass hypotheses; positivity is carefully limited to the stronger SWa1 specialization."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW17",
      "block_sha256": "267f3ab06478769c55963936fe9233ca51e261f73fb5973395e259aeb9a5d5d6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The source rank conditions include even m, m>=2, k>=m+3 and n=k+m-1, giving the stated strict size bounds for both tuple lengths. The original frame Gram determinant is (-1)^(r+1)Tw. All three stabilizer covolumes equal the same ambient c on the supplied setting. Substitution gives c*c=c*c, while both original unipotent covolume-one antecedents are preserved in the generic InVolumesAt statement."
    },
    {
      "id": "SVW18",
      "block_sha256": "76d8389a7cd9d69b6ea6e8f735936e1a53b4471785214d091c3a4e5b02f0c359",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The actual GMR19 MeasCompat-psi contains the compatible orbit measures for both words and every nondegenerate auxiliary X0, and already contains the unipotent covolume-one equations. The literal inVolumes_of_compat consumer therefore discharges every measure antecedent on that same rescaled setting with one character. Original bridge and infinity measures are unchanged; only the three InVolumes fields are claimed, not the remaining mass-data or spectral package."
    }
  ],
